1
00:00:00,110 --> 00:00:03,260
Today, we will be making just a simple bucket
hat.

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:08,420
For this project, I'm going to be using a
5 millimeter hook, a yarn needle, and some

3
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:10,420
white acrylic yarn.

4
00:00:10,420 --> 00:00:13,710
The first thing we're going to do is make
a magic ring or circle.

5
00:00:13,710 --> 00:00:17,340
So, grab your tail end and hold it at the
bottom of your hand.

6
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:20,170
Leave a few inches so you can weave it in
nicely.

7
00:00:20,170 --> 00:00:27,070
Grab the top, wrap it around two fingers to
form an X, and then use your hook to go under

8
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:32,540
and over and pull through.

9
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:39,170
And then use your two fingers to grab the
loop and remove your fingers and then we're

10
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:40,990
going to chain two.

11
00:00:40,990 --> 00:00:48,110
To chain, yarn over and pull through.

12
00:00:48,110 --> 00:00:53,260
Again yarn over and then pull through.

13
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:57,340
And then we're going to do 10 double crochets
into the center of this ring.

14
00:00:57,340 --> 00:01:02,899
And to double crochet, yarn over.

15
00:01:02,899 --> 00:01:10,190
insert your hook into the center of the ring,
yarn over, pull through, yarn over, pull through

16
00:01:10,190 --> 00:01:15,670
just two loops, and then yarn over and pull
through your last two loops.

17
00:01:15,670 --> 00:01:20,650
And then you can tighten the ring by pulling
on the tail end so it's easier to work with.

18
00:01:20,650 --> 00:01:29,799
And again, to double crochet yarn over, insert
your hook, yarn over, pull through, yarn over,

19
00:01:29,799 --> 00:01:35,770
pull through just two loops, and then yarn
over and pull through your last two.

20
00:01:35,770 --> 00:01:41,670
So we're going to do this 8 more times until
we have a total of 10 double crochets.

21
00:01:41,670 --> 00:01:46,430
And now that we are done with our 10 double
crochets, we can pull on the tail end and

22
00:01:46,430 --> 00:01:48,600
close up this little hole.

23
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:56,509
So, we'll just pull really tight and later
on we'll have to tie into a knot so it doesn't

24
00:01:56,509 --> 00:01:59,190
come loose again.

25
00:01:59,190 --> 00:02:03,840
And now we're going to do a slip stitch into
our very first double crochet.

26
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:08,960
So just look for the post of our very first
double crochet, make sure you skip the chain

27
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:17,690
two that we did, and to the right of the post
we're going to go under the 2 loops that make

28
00:02:17,690 --> 00:02:23,690
the V at the top.

29
00:02:23,690 --> 00:02:30,260
And then we're going to yarn over, pull through,
and pull through the loop on our hook and

30
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:32,230
this is a slip stitch.

31
00:02:32,230 --> 00:02:38,349
And we're going to end every round with a
slip stitch and we are also going to start

32
00:02:38,349 --> 00:02:41,230
every round with a chain two.

33
00:02:41,230 --> 00:02:43,290
So for round two, we're going to chain two

34
00:02:43,290 --> 00:02:51,629
and this round we're going to be doing an
increase in every single stitch.

35
00:02:51,629 --> 00:02:58,459
So an increase is just two double crochets
into one stitch and our first stitch is going

36
00:02:58,459 --> 00:03:03,019
to be that same stitch that we slip stitched
into.

37
00:03:03,019 --> 00:03:11,690
So we're going to yarn over, insert our hook
into that same stitch,

38
00:03:11,690 --> 00:03:17,000
and then we'll complete our double crochet.

39
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:21,140
And since we're doing an increase in every
stitch, we're going to do one more double

40
00:03:21,140 --> 00:03:26,050
crochet into that same stitch.

41
00:03:26,050 --> 00:03:31,610
Now we're going to move on to the next stitch
and remember to keep going under both loops

42
00:03:31,610 --> 00:03:37,330
that make the V. And we'll do an increase
into every single stitch.

43
00:03:37,330 --> 00:03:42,569
So here we've done 1 and we're going to do
another one into that same stitch.

44
00:03:42,569 --> 00:03:47,239
And we'll do this all the way around and we
should have 20 stitches by the end of this

45
00:03:47,239 --> 00:03:48,239
round.

46
00:03:48,239 --> 00:03:54,549
Now that we've done our 20 double crochets
for round two, we can slip stitch and start

47
00:03:54,549 --> 00:03:58,209
round three with two chains.

48
00:03:58,209 --> 00:04:03,610
And for round three we're going to do an increase
in every second stitch so in the first stitch

49
00:04:03,610 --> 00:04:23,570
we're going to do 1 double crochet, and then
we'll increase in the second stitch

50
00:04:23,570 --> 00:04:28,110
And then we'll continue this pattern of doing
an increase in every second stitch all the

51
00:04:28,110 --> 00:04:29,330
way around.

52
00:04:29,330 --> 00:04:34,621
And for every round that we do increases in
we're always going to end the round with an

53
00:04:34,621 --> 00:04:40,240
increase, so for the very last stitch make
sure that it ends on an increase; otherwise,

54
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:43,310
it means that you may have counted your stitches
wrong.

55
00:04:43,310 --> 00:04:47,280
And by the end of this round you should have
a total of 30 stitches.

56
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:49,550
So we're increasing every round by 10.

57
00:04:49,550 --> 00:04:55,400
The first round had 10, the second has 20,
and the third has 30.

58
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:59,740
And for round 4, we're going to be increasing
in every third stitch.

59
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:02,080
So last round we did every second.

60
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:08,020
This one we're going to every third and the
next one we're going to do every fourth.

61
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:11,650
So fourth round in every third stitch.

62
00:05:11,650 --> 00:05:17,740
So just subtract 1 from the round number and
that's the stitch that you'll be increasing

63
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:18,740
in.

64
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:23,370
So we're just going to do 2 double crochets,
and then in the third stitch we're doing 2

65
00:05:23,370 --> 00:05:26,150
double crochets into that same stitch.

66
00:05:26,150 --> 00:05:30,870
But if you do not want to have to count, here's
a little trick that you can do to know where

67
00:05:30,870 --> 00:05:32,160
to increase.

68
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:37,650
So if you look on your previous round, you
can find the increase and in this stitch right

69
00:05:37,650 --> 00:05:44,940
between those two double crochets of the increase
from last round that is where your increase

70
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:46,170
for this round will be.

71
00:05:46,170 --> 00:05:52,800
And you can see it here and so you know that
that is where we're going to increase.

72
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:58,490
So we'll just double crochet until we find
the increase from last round and here it is.

73
00:05:58,490 --> 00:06:04,750
So in between these two double crochets in
that stitch I'm going to do an increase and

74
00:06:04,750 --> 00:06:10,810
this should increase it all the way around
evenly so that we have 10 increases per round.

75
00:06:10,810 --> 00:06:16,810
And if you go back and count it it should
line up with every third stitch and we're

76
00:06:16,810 --> 00:06:23,250
just going to be increasing in this way until
this circle becomes the circumference of our

77
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:24,410
head.

78
00:06:24,410 --> 00:06:32,230
I found that 7 total rounds would be about
a small, 8 total rounds would be a medium,

79
00:06:32,230 --> 00:06:35,930
and then 9 would be a large.

80
00:06:35,930 --> 00:06:38,699
And I'm just going to be doing a medium.

81
00:06:38,699 --> 00:06:45,430
So fifth round, I'm going to increase in every
fourth stitch and then sixth every fifth stitch

82
00:06:45,430 --> 00:06:52,410
for the seventh round every sixth stitch eighth
round every seventh.

83
00:06:52,410 --> 00:06:58,300
And I've just finished my eight rounds of
increasing and now we're going to stop increasing

84
00:06:58,300 --> 00:07:04,220
and just do one double crochet into every
single stitch all the way around for the next

85
00:07:04,220 --> 00:07:05,560
few rounds.

86
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:10,180
So again these next few rounds are going to
be just one double crochet into every stitch

87
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:13,330
but this first round is going to be a little
bit different.

88
00:07:13,330 --> 00:07:18,840
So we'll chain two, and then when we double
crochet we're going to go into the back loops

89
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:19,840
only.

90
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:26,360
So if you look from the top there are two
lines that form a V we're going to go in between

91
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:30,970
them and only go under the back loops when
we do our double crochets.

92
00:07:30,970 --> 00:07:38,120
And again this round has no increases we're
just doing one double crochet into every stitch

93
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:40,430
in the back loops only.

94
00:07:40,430 --> 00:07:46,490
And you can see that crocheting in the back
loops only forms a sort of fold so this is

95
00:07:46,490 --> 00:07:52,780
the top of the hat where it bends down and
now we're just going to be crocheting the

96
00:07:52,780 --> 00:07:57,360
portion that is between the brim and the top
of the hat.

97
00:07:57,360 --> 00:08:01,020
And it was just for this first round that
we're going under the back loops only.

98
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:05,979
For the next few rounds, we're going to be
going under both loops and we're going to

99
00:08:05,979 --> 00:08:10,889
do just a few rows until we reached the length
that we want.

100
00:08:10,889 --> 00:08:18,330
And in my case I did 6 more rounds for a total
of 7 between the top of the hat and the start

101
00:08:18,330 --> 00:08:19,330
of the brim.

102
00:08:19,330 --> 00:08:23,210
You can make this shorter or longer if you
want.

103
00:08:23,210 --> 00:08:27,780
So I've done seven total rounds between the
top of the hat and the start of the brim and

104
00:08:27,780 --> 00:08:32,919
you can see that it forms this sort of fold
and we're going to be doing a similar thing

105
00:08:32,919 --> 00:08:37,550
for the brim for the first round for the brim
we're going to be working in the front loops

106
00:08:37,550 --> 00:08:43,589
only so we're going to be folding it a different
direction sort of pop out instead of going

107
00:08:43,589 --> 00:08:44,589
in.

108
00:08:44,589 --> 00:08:47,160
So we're going to be going into the front
loops only.

109
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:52,950
So again, if you look from the top you can
see the V's and you want to go under the first

110
00:08:52,950 --> 00:08:55,529
loop instead of going through both.

111
00:08:55,529 --> 00:08:59,880
And for the brim we are going to be doing
a little bit of increasing.

112
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:04,680
We're just going to be picking up where we
left off when we increased the top of the

113
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:05,680
hat.

114
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:12,190
So for example, I did 8 rounds for the top
of my hat, and this first round of the brim

115
00:09:12,190 --> 00:09:18,339
(I'm going to call it my ninth round of increasing
which means 9 minus 1), I'm going to increase

116
00:09:18,339 --> 00:09:20,400
in every eighth stitch.

117
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:25,860
And you can see that going into the front
loops only causes this part to pop out to

118
00:09:25,860 --> 00:09:27,269
start the brim.

119
00:09:27,269 --> 00:09:32,840
And just like we did before every round after
this will not be in the front loops only it

120
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:37,790
will just be under both loops since we do
not need it to bend anymore.

121
00:09:37,790 --> 00:09:43,100
and I'm going to be alternating in rounds
of increasing and just regular rounds and

122
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:45,180
then increasing and regular round.

123
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:51,649
So this next round will be a regular round
with no increases and in the third round of

124
00:09:51,649 --> 00:09:57,360
the brim, I'm going to be doing another increase
round picking up where I left off with the

125
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:59,019
9th increase round.

126
00:09:59,019 --> 00:10:06,310
So this will be the 10th round of increases
which means 10 minus 1, increase in every

127
00:10:06,310 --> 00:10:08,330
ninth stitch.

128
00:10:08,330 --> 00:10:12,120
And I'm going to be repeating this pattern
until I get the length of the brim that I

129
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:13,120
want.

130
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:19,899
And you want to end on an odd number for the
brim because you want to end on an increase

131
00:10:19,899 --> 00:10:24,070
round so the bottom of the brim doesn't curve
in.

132
00:10:24,070 --> 00:10:30,029
So I just did a total of 5 rounds for the
brim just because it is the length of the

133
00:10:30,029 --> 00:10:36,430
brim that I want and you can make it longer
or shorter by adding more rows or less.

134
00:10:36,430 --> 00:10:41,740
Now we can fasten off by chaining one and
cutting off a strand long enough for us to

135
00:10:41,740 --> 00:10:44,910
weave in.

136
00:10:44,910 --> 00:10:50,070
And then we'll use our hook to pull on that
strand of yarn and pull it through and tighten

137
00:10:50,070 --> 00:10:51,070
the knot.

138
00:10:51,070 --> 00:10:55,149
And the last thing to do is weave in all of
our loose ends.

139
00:10:55,149 --> 00:11:02,079
So first, we're going to turn the hat inside
out

140
00:11:02,079 --> 00:11:11,640
and we're going to be weaving in our ends
into the inside of the hat so it's less visible.

141
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:18,550
We're going to start with the very top and
you want to tighten this as much as you can

142
00:11:18,550 --> 00:11:24,200
and then grab your yarn needle and thread
the yarn through the needle.

143
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:35,120
And we're going to tie a knot just so it stays
in place and the hole doesn't loosen.

144
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:48,160
And to tie a knot, I'm just going to go under
a piece of the yarn,

145
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:54,529
wrap the rest of the tail end around it, and
then pull my yarn needle through and that

146
00:11:54,529 --> 00:11:58,710
should create a knot.

147
00:11:58,710 --> 00:12:03,490
And if you want to do it a second time to
double knot it to really secure it then go

148
00:12:03,490 --> 00:12:05,100
for it.

149
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:11,020
And then we're going to try to go under as
many stitches as we can in one direction.

150
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:17,579
So since the stitches are in rounds, I'll
just be going under the stitches in the second

151
00:12:17,579 --> 00:12:24,149
round.

152
00:12:24,149 --> 00:12:30,890
And once I've gone under a few of the stitches,
I'm going to turn around, skip one stitch,

153
00:12:30,890 --> 00:12:34,180
and go under those same stitches once again.

154
00:12:34,180 --> 00:12:41,160
And so if anything tugs on this loose end,
it will have to go in two different directions

155
00:12:41,160 --> 00:12:42,930
and it'll be really secure.

156
00:12:42,930 --> 00:12:51,380
And we can also do this a few more times just
to be really sure that it won't come loose.

157
00:12:51,380 --> 00:12:59,220
Once we're done, we can just cut off the rest
of that loose end and move on to the other

158
00:12:59,220 --> 00:13:01,279
ones.

159
00:13:01,279 --> 00:13:05,700
And where I had to attach a second ball of
yarn, I'm just going to double knot these

160
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:08,770
two strands together.

161
00:13:08,770 --> 00:13:14,390
So before I start weaving in the loose ends,
i want to be sure that they're knotted and

162
00:13:14,390 --> 00:13:16,810
they won't be coming loose.

163
00:13:16,810 --> 00:13:22,960
And then I'll thread it through my needle
and do the same exact thing where i go under

164
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:29,079
a few stitches in one direction and turn around
and then go back under those same stitches.

165
00:13:29,079 --> 00:13:35,380
Once everything is weaved in, I can just cut
off all of the extra pieces of yarn and we

166
00:13:35,380 --> 00:13:36,930
should be finished.

167
00:13:36,930 --> 00:13:40,080
So here is the bucket hat!

168
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:42,540
That is all for this video; I really hope
you enjoyed.

169
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:46,290
Please leave a like if you did and subscribe
if you're new.

170
00:13:46,290 --> 00:13:50,209
And remember to leave comments if you have
any questions at all.

171
00:13:50,209 --> 00:13:59,739
Thank you so much for watching, I'll see you
next time!

